## Delivered

- Eight authenticated, firm-scoped accountant routes: two extraction-review
  reads plus extraction, classification override, correction, duplicate
  decision, document acceptance, and case finalization mutations.
- Antiforgery on every mutation, live server-side user/session/membership
  revalidation, shared empty `404` failures, private response posture, and no
  anonymous or client extraction path.
- A four-part scoped encrypted-content reader beside the existing write
  adapter, using the same firm-and-case key derivation and exposing plaintext
  only through a clearing disposable lease.
- Development-only deterministic provider and workflow wiring with fail-closed
  configuration; deployable Production and Staging hosts refuse because no
  approved production provider or reader ships.
- Static-SSR list, review, T4, medical, duplicate, disagreement, and field
  components. No new interactive component or global render mode was needed.
- Closed T4 and medical browser projections that omit source content, Box 12,
  identifiers from serialization, provider payloads, and unapproved medical
  content while retaining approved provider/patient display PII only on the
  accountant extraction-review surface.
- The seven authorized downstream guards were narrowed to preserve their
  historical baselines while registering each approved T06 addition
  individually. Antiforgery, historical route, and dependency mutations were
  each confirmed to fail their corresponding guard before being restored.

## Scope held

No T07 verification file, cross-module verification behaviour, production
provider, provider SDK, background worker, queue, timer, source-content route,
WebAssembly project, npm tree, CDN asset, global render mode, or
`MapStaticAssets()` path was added. The existing spec 012 review and spec 014
intake surfaces remain unchanged.
